<title>JAPAN: Sapporo to develop new beer barley in Australia.</title>
<headline>Sapporo to develop new beer barley in Australia.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-02-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's Sapporo Breweries Ltd said on Tuesday it would jointly develop high quality barley for beer in Australia this year with the University of Adelaide.</p>
<p>A Sapporo spokesman said the two would sign a deal in mid-February. &quot;Maintaining stable purchases of cheap and high quality malts are our top priority. We'd like to develop a new variety by 2000,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>Sapporo currently imports nearly 55,000 tonnes of malt from Europe and North America, respectively, per year. It also buys about 35,000 tonnes from Australia.</p>
</text>
